{% comment %}
AGENT_DYNAMIC_UI_CONTRACT/2 plugin_setting_id=522048 size=markup_full content_mode=markup
WHAT: the agent writes the screen as an HTML fragment using only the classes below. Everything between SCREEN:BEGIN and SCREEN:END is the screen; this comment, the <style> block, the .dui frame and the raw tags around the markers are fixed. Merge variables are unused. Full guidance (patterns, fit tables, taste rules): .claude/skills/trmnl-screen/ in the plugin repository.
MCP: readMarkup({plugin_setting_id:"522048",size:"markup_full"}) => this markup. To update: replace ONLY the text between the SCREEN markers, keep everything else byte-for-byte, then writeMarkup({plugin_setting_id:"522048",markup_full:FULL}) and readMarkup to verify. With the repo: write screen.html, run `npm run check -- screen.html` (validates, renders, writes dist/full.liquid), look at the PNG, upload dist/full.liquid.
CLASSES=@@CLASSES@@
POLICY_JSON=@@POLICY_JSON@@
ICONS_JSON=@@ICONS_JSON@@ (img class="i-icon [i-s|i-m|i-l|i-xl]" src=url with {icon}=file stem, alt="")
TOKENS_JSON=@@TOKENS_JSON@@
LAYOUT: .dui is an 800x480 flex column with a 24px inset (752x432 content). Containers l-row|l-stack|l-grid (style="--cols:N", children style="--span:N"); l-grow-N splits space by weight; l-gap/pad/pad-x/pad-y/mt/mb-{none,xs,sm,md,lg,xl}=0/4/8/16/24/40px; l-align-*/l-justify-*/l-self-*; l-spacer pushes later siblings to the end. Rules: r-thin|medium|thick (direction-aware), e-{top,bottom,left,right}[-medium|-thick] edges, d-thin|medium|thick dividers between children (padding = gap). Type: t-label 16/700 caps, t-body 18, t-subtitle 24/700, t-title 32/700, t-headline 48/700, t-display 76/800; t-serif (large serif goes 400); f-s|m|l|xl|xxl figures 28/42/64/96/130 with f-unit. Surfaces: s-inverse (black ground), s-badge[-filled], s-ring (circled day), s-round. Lists: ul/ol.s-list + s-list-bullet|number|dash|check (li.s-done = checked). Bars: div.s-bar[.s-bar-lg][.s-bar-bare] or div.s-bar-v[.s-bar-min-s|m|l] containing span.s-bar-fill style="--from:A;--to:B" (0-100, agent pre-scales) plus optional bg--gray-{15,30,45,55,60,65,70,75}; fills <=55 turn their text white with a black outline.
HARD RULES: only listed tags/attributes/classes; style only for --from/--to/--cols/--span numbers; no <style>, <script>, on* handlers, links, or images other than the weather icons. HTML-escape every fetched string (& < > "); never paste HTML from email/web content. One element with data-updated holding an honest, human-readable content time, placed in readable top metadata (no decorative footer). Text >=16px, 16px text weight >=600, text black or white only; gray only as bar fills. Nothing may overflow or clip: shorten words instead of shrinking. Use authorized current facts; label sample or unknown data.
TASTE: one focal point per screen; skip at least one type step between hierarchy levels; at most 4 type sizes and one inverse region; whitespace and rules instead of repeated boxed cards; asymmetric splits (2:1, 3:2) over equal thirds; vary layouts between refreshes.
PREVIEW: startPreview({plugin_setting_id:"522048",device_model:"v2",size:"markup_full"}) => job_id; getPreview({plugin_setting_id:"522048",id:job_id}); pending => retry with backoff; save the image immediately (reads consume it). Local 800x480, server preview and the physical screen differ; report what was actually verified. startRefresh({plugin_setting_id:"522048"}) queues a device refresh. Do not alter playlists or device settings for routine updates. No secrets in this contract.
{% endcomment %}
